, medicine, and the &#x0201c;placebo effect&#x0201d;</source><publisher-loc>Cambridge, U.K. ; New York</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Cambridge University Press</publisher-name><year>2002</year></citation></ref><ref id="b21-mjm11_2p206"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Price</surname><given-names>DD</given-names></name><name><surname>Finniss</surname><given-names>DG</given-names></name><name><surname>Benedetti</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A Comprehensive Review of the Placebo Effect: Recent Advances and Current Thought</article-title><source>Annu Rev Psychol</source><year>2007</year><month>6</month><day>5</day></citation></ref><ref id="b22-mjm11_2p206"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sherman</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Hickner</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Academic physicians use placebos in clinical practice and believe in the mind-body connection</article-title><source>J Gen Intern Med</source><year>2008</year><month>1</month><volume>23</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>7</fpage><lpage>10</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17994270</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b23-mjm11_2p206"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Goldberg</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Leigh</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Quinlan</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The current status of placebo in hospital practice</article-title><source>General Hospital Psychiatry</source><year>1979</year><volume>1</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>196</fpage><lpage>201</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">499792</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b24-mjm11_2p206"><label>24</label><citation ci